<%- ; Defaults for /etc/docker/daemon.json live here rather than in
   ; lisp/src, so the file's contents are readable where the file is
   ; defined. A host adds to them via config.local.yml's docker_daemon
   ; block (e.g. runtimes.nvidia for GPU transcoding); deep-merge
   ; recurses on plists and unions lists, so host config extends these
   ; rather than replacing them.
   ;
   ; Output stays machine-generated. Nothing in checks/ validates JSON,
   ; and a malformed daemon.json fails `systemctl restart docker` --
   ; which this file's rule in targets/debian/Makefile.elp fires on
   ; change, taking every container down with it.
   ;
   ; dns: docker binds a container's upstream resolvers when the
   ; container STARTS, from /etc/resolv.conf as it reads at that
   ; instant, and never revisits them. tailscaled reports Started ~11s
   ; before it writes that file, so containers starting inside the gap
   ; inherit the ISP's resolvers and can never resolve the tailnet
   ; FQDN -- every public_probe_* fails against a healthy service.
   ; Setting dns explicitly removes the race. Tailscale MUST stay
   ; first: it forwards public names upstream, but an ISP resolver
   ; answers NXDOMAIN for MagicDNS names, and NXDOMAIN is a valid
   ; answer, so the list does not fall through to the next entry.
   ; List-union merge keeps base entries first, so a host can append a
   ; fallback but cannot displace it.
-%>
<%= (plist-tree->json-string
      (deep-merge '(:log-driver "journald"
                    :dns ("100.100.100.100"))
                  (getf globals :docker_daemon))) %>
